@C.LINK
Syntax: C.Link [<opts>] <mainobj> [<obj> ...] [<opts>]
Usage : C compiler linker - build an OS-9 module from objects
Opts  :
  -o=<path>  write the linked module to <path>
  -n=<name>  use <name> as the module name
  -e=<num>   set the module edition number
  -M=<size>  add <size> bytes of data memory
  -l=<path>  link with library <path> (up to 5)
  -m         print the linkage map
  -s         print the final symbol addresses
  -b=<name>  make the module callable from BASIC09, entry <name>
  -t         allow static data in a BASIC09 callable module
Note  : links the relocatable objects from c.asm with cstart.r and
        clib.l into an executable module.  Normally run by CC1/CC2.
